WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.095
(ambient music)

00:00:02.095 --> 00:00:03.523
- [Voiceover] In former
times, Europe used to have

00:00:03.523 --> 00:00:07.223
large mammals like the European
wild horse, the auroch,

00:00:07.223 --> 00:00:09.556
and also the European bison.

00:00:10.922 --> 00:00:13.964
We lost the European wild
horse, we lost the auroch.

00:00:13.964 --> 00:00:15.750
Both got extinct.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.583
And we nearly lost the European bison.

00:00:22.257 --> 00:00:24.740
Rewilding Europe is a new
conservation initiative

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.740
in Europe, trying to make
Europe a wilder place.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.485
The bison plays a very important role.

00:00:31.485 --> 00:00:35.290
We say it is a keystone
species in European landscapes.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.484
Because of its grazing
and browsing behavior,

00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:40.753
it has an impact on the
vegetation and the landscape,

00:00:40.753 --> 00:00:44.614
and that brings new species
in the system, in fact.

00:00:44.614 --> 00:00:47.694
(contemplative music)

00:00:47.694 --> 00:00:50.264
We're here in Armenis in Romania.

00:00:50.264 --> 00:00:52.352
These bison that have
been brought here today

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.952
have traveled a few
thousand kilometers by road.

00:00:55.952 --> 00:00:57.109
People from the local community,

00:00:57.109 --> 00:01:00.295
from the municipality, the mayor is here.

00:01:00.295 --> 00:01:02.963
There's a whole community
around Armenis, which, of course,

00:01:02.963 --> 00:01:05.436
is very interested and also excited

00:01:05.436 --> 00:01:07.269
about this initiative.

00:01:08.573 --> 00:01:10.313
The animals get out of the truck,

00:01:10.313 --> 00:01:12.760
they don't run away,
they just hang around.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.584
They put their horns in the ground,

00:01:14.584 --> 00:01:18.286
and they start fighting with each other.

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:23.090
It's their way of trying
to get used to a place.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.546
We release them in small groups

00:01:24.546 --> 00:01:28.713
into a small area, then we
release them into the wild.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:32.768
(ambient piano music)

00:01:33.676 --> 00:01:37.182
Everybody knows Europe having
fantastic cultural heritage,

00:01:37.182 --> 00:01:41.015
but we also have a
beautiful natural heritage.

00:01:41.863 --> 00:01:44.226
It's amazing to see how nature responds,

00:01:44.226 --> 00:01:46.393
and how species come back.

00:01:48.394 --> 00:01:52.275
It would be a tragedy if we
would lose another big mammal.

00:01:52.275 --> 00:01:53.868
What we hope, of course,
as Rewilding Europe,

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:58.290
is that large herds of bison
can roam our landscapes again,

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.290
and people can enjoy it.

